      question, one line of what it buys, and two answers that answer it.
      simmo and ClothesCast already ask exactly this, and Snoozemo now does
      too, so the four apps read alike.

      The old copy was a statement — "Anonymous analytics" over Allow /
      Don't allow — which reads as a setting being operated rather than a
      question being answered. The words "anonymous" and "so bugs get found
      and fixed" both survive the move, so nothing about what is sent or why
      is lost.

